# Backend Context (`dater`)

## Stack
- Spring Boot 3, Java 17, PostgreSQL, Flyway, JPA/Hibernate.
- JWT access + refresh tokens.
- Test stack: JUnit, MockMvc, Testcontainers.

## Domain flows
- Dates: create/update/list; list supports geo radius filtering.
- Attendees: request, accept/reject, cancel while waitlisted.
- Chat: thread-scoped between date owner and accepted attendee.
- Notifications:
  - in-app notifications (`notifications` table)
  - push notifications via Expo when push token exists
  - per-type user preferences
  - deep-link metadata in push payload (`dateId`, `notificationType`)

## Reliability rules
- Core user actions (accept/reject/send message) should not fail solely because notification dispatch fails.
- Keep logging level production-friendly; avoid temporary debug noise.

## Coordination with mobile
- Any backend contract changes must be mirrored in `dater-mobile/lib/api.ts` types and call paths.
- Keep docs cross-links updated:
  - backend details in `docs/`
  - mobile setup in sibling repo `../dater-mobile/docs/`

